      "layering_notes": "San Joaquin County has no county housing trust fund, no county housing bond and no inclusionary ordinance; the County's own capital for multifamily is limited to HUD pass-through funds administered by the Human Services Agency Neighborhood Preservation Division (sjchsa.org), while the regional gap lender is the SJCOG-sponsored San Joaquin Regional Housing Fund and the main voucher and development partner is the Housing Authority of the County of San Joaquin (HACSJ). The County's PLHA five-year plan does not fund multifamily capital, so PLHA is not a County gap source for tax credit deals here; it sustains shelter operations that otherwise compete with HHAP. Stockton, Lodi, Tracy and Manteca receive their own PLHA formula allocations and may use them differently (Pass 3). County allocation figures are from the HCD 2024-2028 PLHA NOFA allocation tables; the 2019-2023 figures and the Activity 6 plan are from the County PLHA public notice (source).",
